From a3b5c6a1ec32837c40ac1528774e6770227749ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Captain Polliwog build <build@captainpolliwog.invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:38:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 39/55] CSS: cascade layers, range media queries, :is() and
 :where()

- @layer blocks apply as unlayered rules in source order (kept as a
  media rule with no query); their relative ordering is not modeled.
  Google's pages put every rule in a layer, so none applied.
- Media Queries 4 range syntax, (width >= 600px) and (400px <= width <
  900px), rewritten into min-/max- features. Strict < and > are taken
  as <= and >=.
- :is() and :where() as :matches(); :where()'s zero specificity is not
  modeled.
